From: steamlink-ps5
Subject: negotiation: advertise remote HID so the host injects controller input

The client config set enable_remote_hid = 0, telling the host the client does
not do remote HID. The host still opened the pad to read its feature reports
(so "hid: host opened pad 0" appeared), but it never injected the gamepad's
input into the game, so the controller did nothing on the PC. We do provide a
HID gamepad via the ScePad provider, so advertise it (= 1).

diff -ru a/src/session/channels/ch_control_negotiation.c b/src/session/channels/ch_control_negotiation.c
--- a/src/session/channels/ch_control_negotiation.c	2026-10-09 11:01:21.565401560 -0700
+++ b/src/session/channels/ch_control_negotiation.c	2026-10-09 11:01:21.577481587 -0700
@@ -133,7 +133,9 @@
     config.n_available_video_modes = 1;
     config.available_video_modes = availableVideoModes;
 
-    PROTOBUF_C_SET_VALUE(config, enable_remote_hid, 0);
+    /* We provide a HID gamepad (ScePad); tell the host we speak remote HID so it
+     * actually injects our controller input instead of only opening the device. */
+    PROTOBUF_C_SET_VALUE(config, enable_remote_hid, 1);
 
     CStreamingClientConfig clientConfig = CSTREAMING_CLIENT_CONFIG__INIT;
 
